From adcf26b1d7ffe00c61a77beccd4bc3dda1a78056 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ultimatejeeves <ultimatejeeves@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 02:25:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/43] JS: GS thread owns its WebGL context; hosted API for
 embedding

- GSH_OpenGLJs creates its WebGL2 context on an OffscreenCanvas in the GS worker (no more
  synchronous GL proxying to the main thread) and presents frames as ImageBitmaps.
- GS handler created asynchronously (a worker creating a WebGL context needs the main thread).
- PH_Js pad handler fed directly by the page; async pause/resume, save/load state, presentation,
  resolution factor, frame limit, volume, EE clock scale; EE PC/disassembly for profiling.
